  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The discourse surrounding the potential vice presidential candidacy of Sufmi Dasco Ahmad, who currently serves as the Deputy Speaker of the Indonesian House of Representatives, has intensified with broad support from various regional Gerindra Party chapters. Local party leadership from regions such as North Kalimantan, Bali, Gorontalo, and Southeast Sulawesi have voiced their backing, emphasizing his leadership capacity and understanding of national issues. Beyond party affiliates, the Confederation of All Indonesian Trade Unions (KSPSI) has also declared support for his candidacy, highlighting his commitment to advocating for labor rights. Proponents from various political sectors argue that his background in the legislature makes him a suitable candidate to assist the President and maintain national stability. These developments follow ongoing public interest regarding potential changes within the executive office and the qualities required to lead amidst current economic and social challenges.",
